WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:01.380
STEPHANIE WONG: This
week, we're talking

00:00:01.380 --> 00:00:03.930
about protecting sensitive
data, choosing the right cloud

00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:06.180
architecture, and KubeCon 2019.

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:08.580
I'm Stephanie, and welcome to
"This Week in Cloud," where

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:11.520
we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:14.160
Cloud data loss prevention is
a powerful service that brought

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:16.830
state-of-the-art data protection
to a variety of workloads

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:18.150
and storage formats.

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:20.610
And now, it's even better
with an easy-to-use UI,

00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:23.370
making those capabilities
available to your security,

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:25.200
compliance, and legal teams.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:26.700
Learn more about
scanning your data,

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:29.430
setting up regular monitoring,
and identifying trends.

00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:31.248
No terminal required.

00:00:31.248 --> 00:00:32.790
Speaking of sensitive
data, it's time

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:35.790
to revisit best practices
for password management.

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:38.490
October is famous for being
National Cybersecurity

00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:39.810
Awareness Month.

00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:42.823
While it can be fun to dress up
as someone else for Halloween,

00:00:42.823 --> 00:00:45.240
it's a lot less fun when someone
dresses up like your bank

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:46.210
account.

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:48.150
So, in honor of
the holiday, Google

00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:50.790
released two white papers
discussing modern password

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:53.460
security for users and
for system designers.

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:55.530
Happy holiday reading.

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:58.140
One size fits most is
not a policy we believe

00:00:58.140 --> 00:00:59.860
works for cloud solutions.

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:02.040
That's why Google Cloud
offers a variety of products

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:03.667
in many configurations.

00:01:03.667 --> 00:01:05.459
If you find yourself
caught between Compute

00:01:05.459 --> 00:01:08.490
Engine and Kubernetes
Engine, you're not alone.

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:10.630
We've created two
architecture training paths

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:13.740
so that you can learn more about
virtual machines, containers,

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:16.080
and make the best
choice for you.

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:20.310
And, speaking of Kubernetes,
KubeCon and CloudNativeCon 2019

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:24.218
is happening November 18 to the
21st in San Diego, California.

00:01:24.218 --> 00:01:26.760
If you want to learn more about
cloud solutions of all sorts,

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:28.110
you should come.

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:30.857
Register online today or
on site at the conference.

00:01:30.857 --> 00:01:32.940
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:35.830
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:35.830 --> 00:01:37.060
Have any thoughts or ideas?

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:38.530
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:40.880
We'll see you in the cloud.

